target.body:
Closes #103736

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where users/operators changing gateway hooks or cron config together with a plugin/channel setting could see `getRuntimeConfig()` advance while hook routing and cron RPCs stayed on stale live subsystem references for the duration of a deferred reload.

## Why This Change Was Made

Hot reload now publishes rebuilt hooks/cron/heartbeat state before both channel restart deferral entry points: ordinary channel restarts and plugin `beforeReplace` waits. If a later fallible reload step fails after that early publish, the handler rolls the gateway subsystem state back and stops the newly published cron instance so failed reloads do not leave partial state committed.

Health monitor reloads are committed only after the fallible reload work succeeds. That keeps the old monitor tracked and live during any plugin/channel deferral window, then swaps to the new monitor and stops the old one after state commit.

## User Impact

Gateway hot reloads no longer leave hook routing and cron operations split across old and new config during active-work reload deferrals. Failed reloads also restore the prior live subsystem references instead of keeping a partially applied hooks/cron state.

## Evidence

### Real behavior proof — standalone live transcript (exact head `58954a46c6`)

A standalone harness (run with `node --import tsx`, **not** vitest) drives the **real** `createGatewayReloadHandlers` / `applyHotReload` production function against a **real** mutable gateway state (real `getState`/`setState` reference tracking), the **real** `resolveHooksConfig` resolver, and the **real** `buildGatewayCronService` builder. Only the external channel start/stop boundary is injected — exactly the boundary production wiring injects. It prints the actual object references the production code publishes at each lifecycle phase.

```
$ node --import tsx scripts/reload-transaction-proof.ts
================================================================
 GATEWAY HOT-RELOAD SUBSYSTEM TRANSACTION — REAL BEHAVIOR PROOF
 PR #103880 / issue #103736
 REAL applyHotReload + REAL resolveHooksConfig + REAL
 buildGatewayCronService; real getState/setState references.
================================================================

--- Scenario 1: hooks+cron coherence through the deferral window ---
    · before applyHotReload                          hooks=OLD_HOOKS   cron=OLD_CRON
    · inside stopChannel (deferral/restart entry)    hooks=rebuilt#1   cron=rebuilt#2
    · still coherent 50ms into the window            hooks=rebuilt#1   cron=rebuilt#2
    · inside startChannel (deferral/restart entry)   hooks=rebuilt#1   cron=rebuilt#2
    · after applyHotReload (committed)               hooks=rebuilt#1   cron=rebuilt#2
  [PASS] at the deferral entry the published hooks & cron are the NEW rebuilt refs (no stale window)
  [PASS] the SAME new hooks & cron refs stay live all the way through the deferral window
  [PASS] commit keeps those same new hooks & cron refs

--- Scenario 2: forced channel start failure -> rollback ---
    · before applyHotReload                          hooks=OLD_HOOKS   cron=OLD_CRON
    · inside stopChannel (deferral/restart entry)    hooks=rebuilt#3   cron=rebuilt#4
    · inside startChannel (deferral/restart entry)   hooks=rebuilt#3   cron=rebuilt#4
    · after applyHotReload (rolled back)             hooks=OLD_HOOKS   cron=OLD_CRON
    observed: threw=true  OLD_CRON.stopped=true  OLD_CRON.restarted=true
  [PASS] the forced later failure propagates out of applyHotReload
  [PASS] after rollback the live hooks & cron refs are the ORIGINAL prior instances
  [PASS] rollback restarts the prior cron instance

================================================================
 RESULT: ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED
================================================================
```

- **Coherence (Scenario 1):** the rebuilt hooks + cron references are published **before** the channel-restart deferral entry and stay the *same* live references through the async deferral window and through commit — there is no stale-reference window while work drains.
- **Rollback (Scenario 2):** a forced later channel-start failure restores the live hooks + cron references to the **original prior instances**, stops the rebuilt cron, and restarts the prior cron.
- **Discriminating (not a tautology):** on pre-fix code the subsystem state is published only *after* the channel restart, so Scenario 1's "deferral entry = new refs" observation is `OLD_*` and the assertion fails. The RED vitest test below captures the same pre-fix window.

<details>
<summary>Harness source (scripts/reload-transaction-proof.ts — copy/paste to reproduce)</summary>

```ts
/**
 * Standalone real-behavior proof for the gateway hot-reload subsystem transaction
 * (PR #103880 / issue #103736). NOT a vitest test — drives the REAL
 * createGatewayReloadHandlers/applyHotReload with the REAL resolveHooksConfig and
 * REAL buildGatewayCronService against a real mutable getState/setState state.
 * Run: node --import tsx scripts/reload-transaction-proof.ts
 */
import { createGatewayReloadHandlers } from "../src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.js";
import type { OpenClawConfig } from "../src/config/types.openclaw.js";

type AnyRec = Record<string, unknown>;
const delay = (ms: number) => new Promise<void>((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));

let autoSeq = 0;
const tags = new WeakMap<object, string>();
function tag<T extends object>(obj: T, label: string): T {
  if (!tags.has(obj)) tags.set(obj, label);
  return obj;
}
function idOf(obj: unknown): string {
  if (obj === null) return "null";
  if (obj === undefined) return "undefined";
  if (typeof obj !== "object") return String(obj);
  const o = obj as object;
  if (!tags.has(o)) tags.set(o, `rebuilt#${++autoSeq}`);
  return tags.get(o)!;
}
function makeCron(label: string) {
  const cron = {
    started: false,
    stopped: false,
    async start() { cron.started = true; },
    stop() { cron.stopped = true; },
  };
  return tag(cron, label);
}
const line = (s = "") => process.stdout.write(`${s}\n`);

const nextConfig = {
  hooks: { enabled: true, token: "proof-token-xxxxx", path: "/hooks/new" },
  cron: { enabled: false },
  session: { store: "C:/tmp/proof-active-sessions.json" },
} as unknown as OpenClawConfig;
const OLD_HOOKS = tag({ basePath: "/hooks/old", token: "old-token" }, "OLD_HOOKS");
const silentLog = { info: () => {}, warn: () => {}, error: () => {} };

type Obs = { phase: string; hooks: string; cron: string };
const obs: Obs[] = [];
function record(getState: () => AnyRec, phase: string) {
  const st = getState();
  obs.push({ phase, hooks: idOf(st.hooksConfig), cron: idOf((st.cronState as AnyRec)?.cron) });
}

function buildScenario(opts: { failOnStart?: boolean; deferWindowMs?: number }) {
  const oldCron = makeCron("OLD_CRON");
  let state: AnyRec = {
    hooksConfig: OLD_HOOKS,
    hookClientIpConfig: tag({ kind: "old-ip" }, "OLD_IP"),
    heartbeatRunner: { stop: () => {}, updateConfig: () => {} },
    cronState: { cron: oldCron, storePath: "/tmp/old-cron.json", cronEnabled: false, stopExitWatchers: () => {} },
    channelHealthMonitor: null,
  };
  const getState = () => state;
  const setState = (s: AnyRec) => { state = s; };
  const stopChannel = async () => {
    record(getState, "inside stopChannel (deferral/restart entry)");
    if (opts.deferWindowMs) {
      await delay(opts.deferWindowMs);
      record(getState, `still coherent ${opts.deferWindowMs}ms into the window`);
    }
  };
  const startChannel = async () => {
    record(getState, "inside startChannel (deferral/restart entry)");
    if (opts.failOnStart) throw new Error("forced channel start failure (proof)");
  };
  const handlers = createGatewayReloadHandlers({
    deps: {} as never,
    broadcast: () => {},
    getState: getState as never,
    setState: setState as never,
    startChannel: startChannel as never,
    stopChannel: stopChannel as never,
    stopPostReadySidecars: async () => {},
    reloadPlugins: (async () => ({ restartChannels: new Set<string>(), activeChannels: new Set<string>() })) as never,
    logHooks: silentLog as never,
    logChannels: silentLog as never,
    logCron: silentLog as never,
    logReload: silentLog as never,
    createHealthMonitor: (() => null) as never,
  });
  return { handlers, oldCron, getState };
}

const plan = {
  changedPaths: ["hooks", "cron"], restartGateway: false, restartReasons: [], hotReasons: ["hooks", "cron"],
  reloadHooks: true, restartGmailWatcher: false, restartCron: true, restartHeartbeat: false,
  restartHealthMonitor: false, reloadPlugins: false, restartChannels: new Set(["whatsapp"]),
  disposeMcpRuntimes: false, noopPaths: [],
} as AnyRec;

let failures = 0;
function assert(cond: boolean, msg: string) { line(`  [${cond ? "PASS" : "FAIL"}] ${msg}`); if (!cond) failures++; }
function dump() { for (const o of obs) line(`    · ${o.phase.padEnd(46)} hooks=${o.hooks.padEnd(11)} cron=${o.cron}`); }

async function main() {
  line("================================================================");
  line(" GATEWAY HOT-RELOAD SUBSYSTEM TRANSACTION — REAL BEHAVIOR PROOF");
  line(" PR #103880 / issue #103736");
  line(" REAL applyHotReload + REAL resolveHooksConfig + REAL");
  line(" buildGatewayCronService; real getState/setState references.");
  line("================================================================");

  line(""); line("--- Scenario 1: hooks+cron coherence through the deferral window ---");
  {
    const s = buildScenario({ deferWindowMs: 50 });
    obs.length = 0;
    record(s.getState, "before applyHotReload");
    await s.handlers.applyHotReload(plan as never, nextConfig);
    record(s.getState, "after applyHotReload (committed)");
    dump();
    const entry = obs.find((o) => o.phase.includes("stopChannel"));
    const mid = obs.find((o) => o.phase.includes("into the window"));
    const committed = obs.find((o) => o.phase.includes("committed"));
    const newHooks = entry?.hooks, newCron = entry?.cron;
    assert(newHooks !== "OLD_HOOKS" && newCron !== "OLD_CRON", "at the deferral entry the published hooks & cron are the NEW rebuilt refs (no stale window)");
    assert(mid?.hooks === newHooks && mid?.cron === newCron, "the SAME new hooks & cron refs stay live all the way through the deferral window");
    assert(committed?.hooks === newHooks && committed?.cron === newCron, "commit keeps those same new hooks & cron refs");
  }

  line(""); line("--- Scenario 2: forced channel start failure -> rollback ---");
  {
    const s = buildScenario({ failOnStart: true });
    obs.length = 0;
    record(s.getState, "before applyHotReload");
    let threw = false;
    try { await s.handlers.applyHotReload(plan as never, nextConfig); } catch { threw = true; }
    record(s.getState, "after applyHotReload (rolled back)");
    dump();
    const after = s.getState();
    line(`    observed: threw=${threw}  OLD_CRON.stopped=${s.oldCron.stopped}  OLD_CRON.restarted=${s.oldCron.started}`);
    assert(threw, "the forced later failure propagates out of applyHotReload");
    assert(after.hooksConfig === OLD_HOOKS && (after.cronState as AnyRec).cron === s.oldCron, "after rollback the live hooks & cron refs are the ORIGINAL prior instances");
    assert(s.oldCron.started, "rollback restarts the prior cron instance");
  }

  line(""); line("================================================================");
  line(` RESULT: ${failures === 0 ? "ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED" : `${failures} ASSERTION(S) FAILED`}`);
  line("================================================================");
  process.exit(failures === 0 ? 0 : 1);
}
void main();
```

</details>

